click-odoo-update: add ``--watcher-prioritize-update``. With it, the lock watcher never terminates the update: it terminates the sessions that wait for the update longer than ``--watcher-max-seconds``, so they don't exhaust the Odoo workers, and the sessions that keep the update waiting for a lock longer than 1 second, so Odoo doesn't cancel it on lock timeout. In a deadlock with the update, PostgreSQL cancels the other sessions, which Odoo retries, when the database user may raise ``deadlock_timeout`` for the update connections; otherwise the watcher terminates them at once. Requires Odoo 16 or later.
